# Windows PowerShell's parser does not reliably terminate here-strings in an
# LF-only file — it reports a bogus "string is missing the terminator" that
# cascades into unrelated brace errors elsewhere in the script. Force CRLF so
# a checkout on Windows is parseable.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf

# .ps1 must stay ASCII: Windows PowerShell 5.1 decodes it as ANSI without a
# BOM, so a UTF-8 em-dash arrives as bytes the tokenizer reads as a quote.
